\title{arcstat: Arc-Length Statistics, Equivalence Families and Induction Curves}
\description{
Inference from the arc length of statistical functions, and the curves of the induction-period standards. A goodness-of-fit test based on the arc length of the probability plot with an analytic saddlepoint null; distributions built from the arc length of their defining curve, estimated by L-moments; the characteristic-function arc length; a Bayesian nonparametric arc-length test; the equivalence families of the four-parameter kappa distribution of Hosking (1994) \doi{10.1147/rd.383.0251} and of the beta-companion family, on which the two standard induction-period readings coincide; and batched fits, bootstraps and permutation tests of induction curves. One pure-C back-end, parallel by 'OpenMP', serves this package and the 'Python' package 'arcstat'.
